# Database — GORM model associations

Every foreign-key column `XxxID` has a matching association field of the same stem (without the `ID` suffix) pointing at the related model, so `Preload` / `Joins` work without extra wiring.

```go
OrderTypeID int        `gorm:"type:int;not null"`
OrderType   *OrderType `gorm:"foreignKey:OrderTypeID;references:ID"`

OwnerID uuid.UUID `gorm:"type:uuid;not null;index"`
Owner   *User     `gorm:"foreignKey:OwnerID;references:ID"`
```

## Rules

- Use pointer association fields (`*OrderType`) so unloaded relations stay `nil`.
- Add useful inverse sides when needed (has-one / has-many), e.g. `User.Orders []Order` with `foreignKey:OwnerID`.
- Do not model associations to tables outside the app schema with no local Go type (e.g. `auth.users` under Supabase Auth).
- Non-SQL links (encrypted refs, opaque tokens) are **not** foreign keys → no GORM association.
- Keep `database/model/*.go` free of explanatory comments — SQL + these rules are enough.

## Anti-patterns

- FK column without a relation field (`OrderTypeID` alone)
- Value association fields that look "loaded" when zero-valued
- Inventing associations for encrypted / non-joinable refs
